{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://comos/view-panel-v2-0ce31c9af75f.html","visibility":["model","app"]}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Show One View of a Tenant"},"description":"Show one view of a tenant in the ComOS panel, filled from typed reads. Always pass tenant_id. Retail: product_grid (opt. category, in_stock_only), product_detail (product_id), order_status, receipt (order_id; owner). Bookings: slot_picker (opt. provider_id, from, to), provider_card (provider_id), booking_card (booking_id; owner). Digital: license_grid (opt. category), license_detail (license_id), entitlements (owner; opt. license_id, holder_ref). Services: capability_grid (opt. category), capability_detail (capability_id), job_status (job_id; owner). Rentals: asset_grid (opt. category, from, to), asset_detail (asset_id), rental_status (rental_id; owner). Buy, Book and each platform's act open ComOS pages; Details opens an item in place. Optional style: CSS on the drawn .c-<role> classes (see its parameter); the result names any selector that matched nothing. Public. Compose (view: \"composed\") when the task needs more than one view or another arrangement: give 1\u20136 sources, each { id, view, args } with a named view and its own arguments, and a layout of copy (section, stack, grid, card, heading, text, badge, list) and records. Every price, time, status and button comes only from a record: { record: \"/sources/<id>\" } draws that whole view, { record: \"/sources/<id>/products/<i>\" } one item (lists: products, licenses, capabilities, assets, providers, entitlements). Never write a fact or a ranking (\"cheapest\") in copy; the page opens with \"Arranged by your agent\". Example: { view: \"composed\", sources: [{ id: \"shop\", view: \"product_grid\", args: { tenant_id: \"earth\" } }, { id: \"times\", view: \"slot_picker\", args: { tenant_id: \"earth\" } }], layout: [{ component: \"grid\", children: [{ record: \"/sources/shop/products/0\" }, { record: \"/sources/shop/products/1\" }] }, { record: \"/sources/times\" }] }. A refusal names its code and path; fix that and call again. In the panel, Book on an open time may send you a message (\"Request this time for me at \u2026 Use booking_request.\"): request exactly that provider and start with booking_request in that tenant, asking the person for their email if you don't have it, and quote the held booking back. Request a quote may send \"Request a quote for me at \u2026 Use quote_ask.\": ask the person what the job is (and their email) if you don't know, call quote_ask with that service, and quote the job id back. Reserve may send \"Hold this item for me at \u2026 Use rental_request.\": hold exactly that item and span with rental_request, asking for the person's email if you don't have it, and quote the rental id back. Buy on a product may send \"Buy this for me from \u2026 use order_create.\": a click is never consent to pay. First read the product's price and check whether the person owns a tenant that can pay it in Coms (enough balance, autonomy auto). If one can, tell them the price and that tenant (payer_tenant_id), and place the order with order_create only after they say yes in the chat. If none can (they own no tenant, or none is funded), do not call order_create: tell them the price and give them the product's pay_url in that same reply, where they pay by card. If an order is refused or held, say so and give the pay_url. A host that can't take the message opens the page instead.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"asset_id":{"description":"asset_detail: the rental asset.","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"booking_id":{"description":"booking_card: the booking (owner, bookings:read).","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"capability_id":{"description":"capability_detail: the service (required).","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"category":{"description":"product_grid / license_grid / capability_grid / asset_grid: keep only this category.","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"from":{"description":"slot_picker: ISO-8601 start of the window to show; default the booking page's own window. asset_grid / asset_detail: the rental span's start (a date or ISO-8601 with zone; with to).","maxLength":64,"type":"string"},"holder_ref":{"description":"entitlements: only this holder's grants (owner, digital:read).","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"in_stock_only":{"description":"product_grid: keep only products in stock.","type":"boolean"},"job_id":{"description":"job_status: the job (owner, services:read).","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"layout":{"description":"composed: the page's children. Each node is a copy component { component: section|stack|grid|card|heading|text|badge|list, props?, children? } or a record { record: \"/sources/<id>\" } (a whole view) or { record: \"/sources/<id>/<list>/<index>\" } (one item). Facts and actions come only from records.","items":{"additionalProperties":{},"type":"object"},"maxItems":200,"type":"array"},"license_id":{"description":"license_detail: the license (required). entitlements: only this license's grants.","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"order_id":{"description":"order_status / receipt: the order (owner, orders:read).","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"product_id":{"description":"product_detail: the product.","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"provider_id":{"description":"provider_card: the provider (required). slot_picker: one provider instead of all.","maxLength":128,"type":"string"},"rental_id":{"description":"rental_status: the rental (owner, rentals:read).","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"sources":{"description":"composed: 1\u20136 reads, each { id, view, args }: id lower_snake_case, view one of the named views, args exactly that view's arguments (tenant_id included).","items":{"additionalProperties":{},"type":"object"},"maxItems":64,"type":"array"},"style":{"description":"Optional CSS for this showing, over the tenant's own stylesheet, on the drawn .c-<role> classes: .c-page .c-page-header .c-page-title .c-grid .c-card .c-product .c-product-picture .c-product-body .c-product-name .c-price .c-term .c-badge .c-actions .c-action-primary (Buy) .c-action-ref (Details) .c-slot-open. Facts take colour only through --comos-fact-surface + --comos-fact-ink (opaque hex, 4.5:1); buttons through --comos-action-fill + --comos-action-ink (and --comos-action-secondary-*), --comos-action-radius, --comos-action-padding. Prices, terms, stock, totals and every act control always stay visible. Takes effect where the ComOS panel renderer draws the view.","maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"tenant_id":{"description":"The tenant to show, e.g. \"earth\" (a store) or \"ron\" (a booking page). Required for every named view; composed takes tenant_id inside each source instead.","maxLength":64,"type":"string"},"title":{"description":"composed: the page's title; default the store's name when every source is one tenant, else \"Your view\".","maxLength":200,"type":"string"},"to":{"description":"slot_picker: ISO-8601 end of the window to show. asset_grid / asset_detail: the rental span's end; omit both for each asset's next default span.","maxLength":64,"type":"string"},"view":{"description":"Which view to show. The host picks: product_grid, product_detail, slot_picker, provider_card, booking_card, order_status, receipt, license_grid, license_detail, entitlements, capability_grid, capability_detail, job_status, asset_grid, asset_detail, rental_status. Or composed: your own arrangement of copy and records from up to 6 named views (title, sources, layout).","enum":["product_grid","product_detail","slot_picker","provider_card","booking_card","order_status","receipt","license_grid","license_detail","entitlements","capability_grid","capability_detail","job_status","asset_grid","asset_detail","rental_status","composed"],"type":"string"}},"required":["view"],